/* ============================================================
   The application's theme — the only place colour lives.

   The values come from the mock-up this screen was built from and are
   quoted as hex, because the mock-up is their source: a cream
   background, a white card, a dark green accent. A component NEVER
   writes a hex of its own — a raw colour in a component is a token
   nobody has named, and it is invisible to every later change of the
   palette.

   THE DARK THEME WAS WITHDRAWN, and that is a decision rather than an
   oversight: the switch lived in a top bar that no longer exists, and
   the mock-up has a single palette. The reason and the consequences:
   `spec/design/ui/system-states.md` § One palette. It comes back
   together with a mock-up that describes it — and then this file gets
   a second block while the components get not one branch.

   NOTE: `@theme`, not `@theme inline`. `inline` puts the DECLARED
   VALUE straight into the class, so `.text-ink` would set as a
   particular colour and redefining the variable below would stop doing
   anything — silently.
   ============================================================ */

@theme {
  /* ---- Typeface -----------------------------------------------
     Two families and their fallback stacks. The stack is part of the
     token rather than an ornament: a font from the network can fail to
     arrive, and the screen should then look plainer, not disappear. */
  --font-sans: 'Instrument Sans', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
  --font-serif: 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;

  /* ---- Text ---------------------------------------------------- */
  --color-ink: #1b1a17;
  --color-muted: #5c584f;
  /* Darkened from `#9b978c` on 2026-09-16. The old value measured 2.92:1 on a
     white card and 2.54:1 on `--color-surface-medium` -- below AA's 4.5:1 and
     below even the 3:1 large-text floor, so the problem did not go away by
     making the text bigger. It painted the card's own Edit and Delete actions,
     every timestamp, the character counter, the footer, and -- through
     `::placeholder` -- the ONLY label the composer's fields have.
     `--color-muted` measured 7.09:1 throughout, which is what says one token
     was wrong rather than the palette.
     This value is the lightest member of the token's own hue family
     (R = B+15, G = B+11, the relationship `#9b978c` already had) that clears
     4.5:1 against the DARKEST surface this palette paints, `#f1efe8`: 4.69:1
     there, 4.95:1 on the page, 5.40:1 on a card. Lightest on purpose -- the
     token exists to be quieter than `--color-muted`, and every step darker
     spends that distinction. Held by `tests/fitness/test_design_tokens.py` and,
     where it lands on screen, by `e2e/ui/test_smoke.py`. */
  --color-faint: #6e6a5f;
  /* Text of an inactive control, and nothing else. It measures 1.82:1 and stays
     there: WCAG 1.4.3 exempts a disabled control outright. The decision is
     written down in `spec/design/ui/system-states.md` § Tokens and carried as
     the single entry of `PERMITTED_BELOW_FLOOR`, because an exemption nobody
     recorded cannot be told from an oversight. */
  --color-disabled: #c4c0b5;
  --color-inverse: #f6f5f1;
